The source is copied to the stage path above (without .git, build, bin or results),
built there, and the staged source/build tree is removed after the build.
The primary binary is written to bin\; per-toolchain copies stay in bin\ and artifacts\.

Why stage at all? The MinGW Makefiles generator can fail when the source path
contains non-ASCII characters. Staging gives every toolchain an ASCII path.

